ntdll: unix libraries from Tempwind's static table, in place of dlopen
(docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 2, "Unix libraries").

Why: win32u's Unix side is linked into the module, and libc's dlopen
stays unused (its dlerror reaches __get_tp, which stops loudly; stubs.c).

- get_builtin_unix_funcs (L837-863) calls tw_unixlib_funcs(unix_path, wow)
  (native/wine/src/unixlibs.c) in place of dlopen and dlsym, under the
  same virtual_mutex, and returns STATUS_SUCCESS with the funcs it gives.
  A builtin without a unix_path still returns STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND, and an
  unknown module still leaves the list with that status. A wow request or
  a library not in the table stops loudly there. unix_handle stays NULL, so
  release_builtin_module (L789-808) has no handle to dlclose.
- Its only caller is NtQueryVirtualMemory's MemoryWineUnixFuncs and
  MemoryWineUnixWow64Funcs case (L6113), which a builtin DLL's
  __wine_init_unix_call reaches (dlls/winecrt0/unix_lib.c L92-96); the
  handle it stores is the funcs' address, which the unix-call dispatcher
  checks with tw_unixlib_count (section 11).

Line numbers are wine-11.0's dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -875,6 +875,12 @@
 /***********************************************************************
  *           get_builtin_unix_funcs
  */
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+/* Tempwind (wine-unix.md, section 2): the unix libraries are linked into the
+ * module; native/wine/src/unixlibs.c's static table gives their funcs. */
+extern const void *tw_unixlib_funcs( const char *unix_path, int wow );
+#endif
+
 static NTSTATUS get_builtin_unix_funcs( void *module, BOOL wow, const void **funcs )
 {
     const char *ptr_name = wow ? "__wine_unix_call_wow64_funcs" : "__wine_unix_call_funcs";
@@ -886,6 +892,17 @@
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( builtin, &builtin_modules, struct builtin_module, entry )
     {
         if (builtin->module != module) continue;
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+        /* no dlopen or dlsym: unix_handle stays NULL, so release_builtin_module
+         * has nothing to dlclose */
+        (void)ptr_name;
+        if (builtin->unix_path)
+        {
+            *funcs = tw_unixlib_funcs( builtin->unix_path, wow );
+            status = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
+        break;
+#endif
         if (builtin->unix_path && !builtin->unix_handle)
         {
             builtin->unix_handle = dlopen( builtin->unix_path, RTLD_NOW );
